1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,600
Welcome to The Unit, Unusual Schools Around the World. A.

2
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:13,240
Kitty is listening to a programme about some unusual schools.

3
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:22,435
Listen with her and match the picture of each school with its country and the reason for creating it.

4
00:00:22,435 --> 00:00:29,120
Now we are going to learn about some unusual schools around the world.

5
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:32,480
First, let's go to India.

6
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:39,160
Many poor families there do not have enough money to send their children to school.

7
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:52,070
Lots of children have to work at train stations or on trains to help support their families, so some teachers started schools for these children at the station.

8
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:55,700
Now, let's turn to Bangladesh.

9
00:00:55,700 --> 00:01:03,710
Bangladesh often has floods when heavy rains hit the country, but children don't have to miss school.

10
00:01:03,710 --> 00:01:06,840
A school boat picks the children up.

11
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:11,790
They have lessons on the boat, and then the boat takes them home.

12
00:01:11,790 --> 00:01:16,000
Finally, the School of the Air in Australia.

13
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:22,170
Some people live on farms, hundreds of kilometres from the nearest school.

14
00:01:22,170 --> 00:01:29,650
But children in these areas are able to use the internet to talk with their teachers and classmates.
